  "question": {
    "text": "Suppose the family of lines <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> (where <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></math> are in arithmetic progression) be normal to a family of circles. The radius of the circle of the family which intersects the circle <math><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> orthogonally is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "WSpls",
      "text": "<math><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math> units",
